    <sys:String x:Key="FB.Beta" xml:space="preserve">EXPERIMENTAL BETA</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.Intro" xml:space="preserve">Frame generation for the game window you pick, through the public Windows capture APIs. No game modification, no injection, no memory access. FrameBoost captures only that window and shows the doubled output over it. Real, measured numbers only; a value shows N/A rather than a guess when it cannot be measured.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.FrameGeneration" xml:space="preserve">Frame generation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.MainDisplay" xml:space="preserve">Pick the game window, then turn FrameBoost on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.BestResult" xml:space="preserve">For the best result</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.YourMonitor" xml:space="preserve">Your monitor:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.CapAdvice" xml:space="preserve">Cap the game at {0} FPS. FrameBoost doubles it to {1}, which is what a {1} Hz monitor can show.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.GpuRoom" xml:space="preserve">Leave the GPU some room. FrameBoost needs a few milliseconds of GPU time for every frame it generates. If the game already runs the GPU at 100%, lower the resolution or graphics settings until it doesn't.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.SteadyCap" xml:space="preserve">A steady, capped frame rate works much better than an uncapped one that jumps around.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FB.PremiumFeature" xml:space="preserve">FrameBoost is a Premium feature</sys:String>
